BACKEND
[x] Provider API Server
[x] x402 Middleware
[x] Blockchain Service Layer
[x] Registry Gateway API
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOG
* Created express boilerplate server
    - mock API routes
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GETTING STARTED
- after cloning this repository, run the following steps:
    1. Move into backend folder
            cd apps/backend
    2. Install Node.js dependencies (IMPORTANT)
            pnpm install
    3. Run server
            pnpm dev
    4. Test APIs with Curl/Postman
            server_runs_at: http://localhost:3001
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REQUIREMENTS
- Node.js 18+
- pnpm package manager
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEPENDENCIES
- express => HTTP server
- cors => different origin API access
- dotenv => env config
- ethers => blockchain interaction
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEV DEPENDENCIES
-typescript
- ts-node-dev
- @types/node
- @types/express
- @types/cors
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
API ENDPOINTS
    GET /api/btc
        - ret mock btc data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SMART CONTRACT CONNECTION
    - the backend will connect to:
        1. APIRegistry.sol
            PURPOSE
            - store registered APIs
            - retrieve API endpoint & pricing
            - allow discovery for agents & frontend
            TODO:
            * backend will read registry via ethers.js
            * replace local mock registry
        2. X402Facilitator.sol
            PURPOSE
            - verify payments
            - enforce nonce & deadline rules
            - execute USDC transfers
            - unlock API access after settlement
            TODO:
            - backend calls settle() function
            - validates payment before returning API response
